BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brew at the Zoo
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTSTAMP:20260829T151757Z
UID:2f2070c631904a407ca11ec8d953@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Tap into your wild side at Brew at the Zoo on Saturday\, Augus
 t 29th\, an adults-only evening event\, and sample hundreds of beers\, har
 d seltzers\, wines and ready-to-drink cocktails from dozens of local\, reg
 ional and national breweries. This year’s event is bigger and better tha
 n ever with the addition of a brand-new wine tasting experience! Enjoy liv
 e musical entertainment by TJ &amp\; the Campers\, animal encounters\, and
  more at Rhode Island’s largest outdoor beer festival. This is a 21+ eve
 nt\, and no person under the age of 21 will be permitted (including infant
 s). All attendees are required to show a valid ID. Rain or shine\, tickets
  are non-refundable.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/bre
 w-at-the-zoo/110973/
LOCATION:Roger Williams Park Zoo & Carousel Village\, 1000 Elmwood Avenue
 \, Providence\, 02907
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/brew-at-the-zoo/110973/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Celestial Night - Painting Class
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTSTAMP:20260829T151757Z
UID:d21995bcec01b5499363a07ed281@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:🖌️ IN-STUDIO SESSION DETAILS Reserve your spot and enjoy 
 a complimentary beverage—choose from soda\, beer\, or wine (21+ with val
 id ID). Additional drinks will be available for purchase. Immerse yourself
  in a fun and creative atmosphere while painting your own unique masterpie
 ce! Recommended for ages 14 and up. ⏰ ARRIVAL TIME Our studio opens 30 m
 inutes prior to class time. We recommend arriving 15&#8211\;30 minutes ear
 ly to find parking\, grab a drink\, and get settled. Please note: If you a
 rrive late\, the artist may not be able to fill you in on the steps you mi
 ssed\, as they will be focused on guiding the rest of the class. If you ar
 rive more than 20 minutes late\, we kindly ask that you do not join the se
 ssion. Late arrivals can be disruptive and may not have enough time to com
 plete the painting. Unfortunately\, we cannot offer refunds or reschedules
  for late arrivals. 🚗 PARKING INFO Our studio is located at 150 Main St
 reet (rear entrance)\, Pawtucket\, Rhode Island\, and we have two FREE par
 king lots: 🚗 One directly attached to our entrance 🚗 A second lot ju
 st one building down on the same side of the street — clearly labeled 
 🪑 WANT TO SIT WITH FRIENDS? If you purchased 2 or more tickets in one t
 ransaction\, we’ll automatically seat your group together. If you booked
  separately but want to sit with someone\, please include their first and 
 last names in the “Additional Information / Order Notes” field during 
 checkout. 🔄 RESCHEDULING &amp\; CANCELLATION POLICY All reservations ar
 e non-refundable. However\, if you need to reschedule\, you may request a 
 reschedule voucher at least 48 hours before your session. You can do this 
 easily on our website — just [click here]. No-shows cannot be reschedule
 d. 🚨 CLASS CANCELLATION Classes may be canceled due to low attendance. 
 In this case\, we’ll notify you and issue a voucher for a future session
 . We appreciate your understanding and look forward to welcoming you to a 
 future class! ❄️ INCLEMENT WEATHER POLICY Because New England weather 
 can be unpredictable\, we typically wait until a few hours before class to
  make final decisions. If we cancel due to snow or other severe weather\, 
 we’ll email you a voucher for a future session. Have more questions? Che
 ck out our [Frequently Asked Questions] page — just [click here].\n\nSou
 rce: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/celestial-night-painting-class
 /110958/
LOCATION:Paint and Vino\, 150 Main Street\, Pawtucket\, RI 02860
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/celestial-night-painting-class/
 110958/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Charles Esten Solo Acoustic
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260829
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260830
DTSTAMP:20260829T151757Z
UID:d23898d7b6ef6d854567656eb80b@visitri-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Over the last few years\, singer/songwriter and actor Charles 
 Esten - best known for his roles as Ward Cameron on the NETFLIX global hit
  show Outer Banks\, and Deacon Claybourne in ABC/CMT’s Nashville\, has p
 erformed hundreds of live concerts\, including multiple headline tours in 
 the US\, Germany\, Amsterdam\, and UK\, including the Royal Albert Hall. I
 n early 2020\, his main stage performance as part of the popular Country2C
 ountry festival in Europe was cut short by the pandemic. After that\, for 
 over a year during lockdown\, he entertained fans virtually with his weekl
 y FacebookLive Quarantine Livestream drawing over 1.5 million total views.
  He has resumed live performances\, most notably on the Grand Ole Opry\, w
 here he has made over 150 appearances to-date. He was excited to open at T
 he Ryman for Deanna Carter in November 2021. In his adopted hometown of Na
 shville\, Esten serves as the National Honorary Spokesperson for the Leuke
 mia &amp\; Lymphoma Society’s annual “Light The Night” Walk\, and as
  a board member and volunteer for Musicians On Call. When not filming or t
 ouring\, he continues to write and record his own music with over 10 milli
 on streams to date\, and a 2018 Guinness World Record for releasing 54 ori
 ginal songs (available on iTunes\, and on Spotify) once a week\, for 54 co
 nsecutive weeks. His latest independent release\, as an artist-songwriter 
 launched March 3rd and is called “One Good Move.” The heartfelt romant
 ic rocker sets the tone for his next chapter with his forthcoming debut al
 bum.\n\nSource: https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/charles-esten-solo-
 acoustic/111163/
LOCATION:Stadium Theatre\, 28 Monument Square\, Woonsocket\, RI 02895
URL:https://www.visitrhodeisland.com/event/charles-esten-solo-acoustic/111
 163/
END:VEVENT
